---
Implement arc/radial knob rendering for synth parameters.

Replace flat slider-based knobs with circular arc knobs drawn on Nuklear canvas.
Mouse drag up/down to rotate. Show value label below. Used for volume, pan,
filter cutoff, resonance, ADSR, LFO rate, etc.

## Design
- Draw arc from ~225 degrees to ~315 degrees (270 degree sweep)
- Fill arc proportional to parameter value (0.0 to 1.0)
- Mouse drag: vertical movement maps to value change
- Double-click to reset to default (stretch goal)
- Colors: track color for active arc, dark gray for inactive

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] knob_draw() function in knobs.c that renders arc on canvas
- [ ] Mouse interaction: click-drag vertically to change value
- [ ] Value label below the knob
- [ ] Used in synth editor for at least: cutoff, resonance, attack, release
- [ ] Looks good at different sizes (30px to 60px diameter)

## Test Plan
- [ ] Visual inspection: knobs render correctly at various sizes
- [ ] Interaction: drag produces smooth value changes
- [ ] Edge cases: min/max clamping, rapid drag
